## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design dynamic, per-tenant tracing in a multi-DC docker-dca setup, including config retrieval, TTL-based caching, and graceful degradation when the sidecar cannot fetch config.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry sampling and per-tenant configuration
- Consul KV as a central per-tenant policy store
- TTL caching to limit external calls
- Graceful fallback to sensible default rate
- Cross-DC deployment considerations and observability impact

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-sampler for per-tenant tracing
class TenantSampler {
  constructor(fetchRate) {
    this.fetchRate = fetchRate; // function(tenant) -> rate
    this.cache = new Map(); // tenant -> {rate, expiry}
  }
  getRate(tenant) {
    const entry = this.cache.get(tenant);
    if (entry && entry.expiry > Date.now()) return entry.rate;
    // fetch from Consul KV here, then cache for 5s
    const rate = this.fetchRate(tenant) ?? 20;
    this.cache.set(tenant, { rate, expiry: Date.now() + 5000 });
    return rate;
  }
  shouldSample(tenant) {
    const rate = this.getRate(tenant);
    return Math.random() * 100 < rate;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test correctness of per-tenant rates during rollout?
- What are failure modes if Consul KV is unavailable, and how to mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine TLS edge proxying with per-tenant feature gates loaded from a daemon-managed config source. It also checks bootstrap discipline in a two-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Configs for runtime config
- TLS termination at Nginx edge proxy
- Per-tenant feature gates in a small API
- Simple bootstrap for tenants and flags

## Code Example
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
let flags = {};
function loadFlags() {
  const txt = fs.readFileSync('/etc/feature-flags.yaml','utf8');
  flags = yaml.load(txt) || {};
}
loadFlags();
app.get('/health-quiz', (req, res) => {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (tenant && flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].enabled) res.sendStatus(200);
  else res.sendStatus(403);
});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this gating with CI and two data centers?
- What are failure modes if the config-loader container is unavailable?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests distributed tracing setup across data centers, focusing on OpenTelemetry instrumentation, cross-DC propagation, and dynamic sampling via Docker Config rather than hard-coded values.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry instrumentation and OTLP exporters
- Cross-DC trace propagation with TraceContext
- Docker Config for per-tenant sampling rules
- Traefik TLS termination and service mesh-lite tracing
- Replicated collectors and scalable backends

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: OpenTelemetry setup sketch (Node.js) import and initialization
const { NodeTracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');
const { SimpleSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base');
const { registerInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation');

const provider = new NodeTracerProvider({ /* resource: tenant, service, etc. */ });
const exporter = new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: process.env.OTLP_URL });
provider.addSpanProcessor(new SimpleSpanProcessor(exporter));
provider.register();
registerInstrumentations({ tracerProvider: provider, // instrumentations
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you roll out per-tenant sampling rate changes without redeploying?
- How would you verify trace completeness across DCs during a failover?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical secret lifecycle management in Docker Swarm, integrating Vault for automated rotation with zero-downtime upgrades and proper secret versioning.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm secrets versioning and dynamic reattachment
- Vault-based rotation triggers and secret provisioning
- Rolling updates with start-first strategy to avoid downtime
- Health checks to confirm new secrets are loaded before removing old ones
- Atomic secret updates using add-then-remove pattern

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-automation: rotate Vault-derived Swarm secrets
async function rotateSecrets(serviceName, vaultPath) {
  // Fetch new credentials from Vault
  const newCreds = await vault.read(vaultPath);

  // Create new Swarm secrets
  const newSecrets = await createSwarmSecrets(newCreds);

  // Update service with new secrets
  await updateService(serviceName, newSecrets);

  // Verify health before cleanup
  await verifyServiceHealth(serviceName);

  // Remove old secrets
  await cleanupOldSecrets(serviceName);
}
```
